# Helios agent integration — environment template
#
# Copy to .env, fill in, then load it:
#     cp .env.example .env
#     set -a; source .env; set +a          # bash / zsh
# Then check the connection before running an agent:
#     agent-integration doctor
#
# .env is gitignored; .env.example is not. Nothing here is required: with no
# token at all, `demo`, `selfcheck`, `inspect` and `run --offline` all work,
# and grants are signed with an ephemeral process key.

# --- Model (the action agent) ---------------------------------------------
#
# Qwen, via DashScope's OpenAI-compatible Chat Completion endpoint. The token
# is sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` — plain, exactly as given.
#
# Competition rule: Qwen is the only generative model allowed here.
#
# Accepted variable names, in priority order:
#   HELIOS_LLM_API_KEY, DASHSCOPE_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY
# OPENAI_API_KEY is last because Qwen Code sets it; an explicitly Helios or
# DashScope key always wins so the right quota is spent.
HELIOS_LLM_API_KEY=

# Model id. Anything in the qwen3 family is a hybrid reasoning model, so the
# driver sends `enable_thinking: false` for it (those models default to
# thinking mode and refuse a non-streaming request while it is on). For any
# other model id neither thinking field is sent at all.
HELIOS_LLM_MODEL=qwen3.8-max

# Endpoint. Leave this at the public URL UNLESS your token came from a gateway.
# A gateway issues its own base URL, and the public one will reject its token
# with a 401.
#
# Accepted variable names, in priority order:
#   HELIOS_LLM_BASE_URL, OPENAI_BASE_URL
# Override with `--base-url` on the command line if you prefer.
HELIOS_LLM_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1

# Output cap per turn. An agent turn is a tool call or a short sentence, so
# 4096 is plenty and much cheaper than the model maximum.
HELIOS_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=4096

# --- Audit signing ---------------------------------------------------------
# The audit agent signs every grant with HMAC-SHA256. Without this key it
# falls back to an ephemeral process key: the replay and tamper checks still
# run, but grants do not survive a restart and two processes cannot verify
# each other. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
HELIOS_AUDIT_SIGNING_KEY=

# A label recorded on grants so you can tell which key signed what. This is
# never the key itself.
HELIOS_AUDIT_SIGNING_KEY_ID=helios-audit-local
